            |P/1869    G1|1869      I| 1869a|1869-04-09|F.A.Th. Winnecke
# P.F.A. Méchain discovered this comet in the evening sky near Omicron Piscium on 1790
# January 9.75. H.P. Tuttle discovered this comet on 1858 January 5.01. Ch. W. Tuttle
# used three positions obtained between January 5 and 13, and computed a parabolic orbit
# with a perihelion date of 1858 February 20.48 and a perihelion distance of 1.070 AU.
# He noted "so strong a resemblance to [the orbit] of the second comet of 1790, that
# there would seem to be small reason for doubt of the identity of the comet."
          8P|P/1858    A1|1858      I|      |1858-01-05|H.P. Tuttle
